
 ====================================================================
  RELAY NINE :: RECOVERY SHELL
 ====================================================================

  Relay Nine went dark mid-shift. Six operators each held one segment
  of the station, and each one sealed their segment behind their own
  account on the way out. The handover keys were never collected.

  You are the recovery operator. Work forward one segment at a time:
  the key material inside segment N is the SSH password for segment
  N+1. Segment 5 holds the trophy flag that closes the station out.

 --------------------------------------------------------------------
  HOW TO PLAY
 --------------------------------------------------------------------

   ghost-brief     what this segment wants from you (prints on login)
   ghost-next      the exact ssh command for the next segment
   ghost-submit    check the trophy flag once you reach the end

  Moving on:   ssh level<N+1>@localhost -p 2222
               ...or log out and ssh in from your own terminal.

 --------------------------------------------------------------------
  GROUND RULES
 --------------------------------------------------------------------

   *  Everything you need is already installed. The relay has no
      route to the internet and does not need one.
   *  Your home directory is readable but not writable. That is
      deliberate — nobody can break their own puzzle. Use /tmp for
      scratch work.
   *  No segment can read another segment's home directory. If you
      find yourself trying, you are off the intended path.
   *  Brute-forcing the SSH passwords, attacking sshd, or trying to
      reach root is out of scope. The keys are all findable.
   *  Stuck? Re-read the brief, then read the manual page for the
      tool it names. `man find`, `man base64`, `man xxd`.

  Good hunting, operator.

